<article class="env-corollary" id="D68BB7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D68BB7">Corollary <span data-tag="D68BB7">4.3.1.16</span>.</a> Let $p: \calC \rightarrow \calE $ be a Cartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories, $E \in \calE $ an object, and $\overline{f}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC _{E}$ a diagram. Then $\overline{f}$ is a colimit diagram in $\calC _{E}$ if and only if it is a $p$-colimit diagram in $\calC $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a href="/tag/973887" data-tag="973887">4.3.1.15</a> in the case where $\calD = \calE $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>